DTDT white sheet — high-level spec

1. Purpose

DTDT (Dual-Time Distributed Telescope) is a containerized, self-healing compute system that:

Ingests multi-instrument telescope telemetry (JWST, HST, etc.).

Runs dual-time cosmological kernels (forward, reverse, predictive).

Streams real-time state and forecasts to a live dashboard.

Operates on a multi-node, GPU-aware, auto-recovering worker mesh.

2. Core layers

1. Physics & math layer

Standard cosmological field equations and lookback integration.

Smooth sigmoid multi-loss functions for stable optimization.

Dual-time modes:

FORWARD: standard evolution.

REVERSE: reconstruction/retrodiction.

PREDICTIVE: autoregressive trajectory forecasting.

2. Telemetry ingestion layer

Adapters: adapters/jwst.py, adapters/hst.py, etc.

Config: telemetry_sources.yaml (endpoints, formats, filter→wavelength maps).

All adapters output a single type:

NormalizedTelemetry = {
    "instrument": str,
    "exposure_id": str,
    "timestamp_utc": str,
    "ra_deg": float,
    "dec_deg": float,
    "wavelength_nm": float,
    "flux": list[float],
    "metadata": dict,
}

3. Compute & orchestration

1. Job model (Redis-backed)

Global queues by priority:

dtdt:jobs:CRITICAL | SCIENCE | REPLAY | LOW

Job payload fields (JSON):

{
  "jobId": "run_...",
  "fitsPath": "...",
  "cosmoConfigPath": "...",
  "source": "JWST",
  "priority": "CRITICAL",
  "timeMode": "FORWARD|REVERSE|PREDICTIVE",
  "requiresGPU": false,
  "preferredZone": "us-central-1a",
  "retry": {
    "maxAttempts": 5,
    "backoffStrategy": "exponential",
    "initialDelayMs": 1000,
    "maxDelayMs": 60000
  }
}

2. Worker layer (NodeJS)

Pulls jobs from Redis queues in priority order.

Spawns Python engine (engine/run_dtdt.py or real engine).

Tracks status in dtdt:job:<jobId>:status:

state, attempts, nodeId, workerId, timestamps, errors.

Retry logic with backoff; dead-letter queue:

dtdt:jobs:dead-letter, dtdt:dead:<jobId>:*.

3. Multi-node cluster

Shared Redis/cluster as coordination fabric.

Node metadata:

dtdt:nodes (SET of nodeIds)

dtdt:nodes:<nodeId>:info (HASH: zone, capacity, gpuCount, labels)

dtdt:nodes:<nodeId>:heartbeat (STRING timestamp)

dtdt:nodes:<nodeId>:runningJobs (SET of jobIds)

Orchestrator process:

Detects dead nodes via heartbeat timeout.

Requeues orphaned jobs from runningJobs.

Cleans node registry.

4. GPU acceleration layer

Config: DTDT_USE_GPU, DTDT_GPU_BACKEND, DTDT_GPU_DEVICE.

engine/gpu_core.py dispatches CPU vs GPU kernels.

GPU kernels accelerate lookback integration and heavy vector ops.

4. Engine behavior

1. Main loop

Input: NormalizedTelemetry, cosmology config, TimeMode.

Maintains StateHistory (loss, vel, acc over steps).

Emits transitions:

{
  "step": 42,
  "loss": 0.031,
  "vel": -0.004,
  "acc": 0.001,
  "predictive": {
    "horizon_steps": 16,
    "predicted_loss": [...],
    "confidence": 0.82
  }
}

2. Predictive mode

Autoregressive fit on recent loss (and extendable to full phase-space).

Produces short-horizon forecasts + confidence.

Sent to dashboard for overlay.

5. Observability & failure handling

Status keys per job (running, retry-scheduled, completed, dead-letter, orphaned).

Dead-letter schema for forensic inspection:

payload, error, attempts, priority, timestamps, instrument.

Mock runner (engine/run_dtdt.py) for safe pipeline testing.

6. Interfaces

Northbound: web dashboard (WebSocket/HTTP) consuming transition streams and job status.

Southbound: telescope archives (FITS/HDF5), object storage, GPU/CPU nodes.

Control plane: Redis + orchestrator + worker cluster.

